# Cronie. crond holds no client connections and reloads nothing on its own, so
# an upgrade moves it onto the new program straight away, and a removal stops it
# rather than leaving a scheduler running from an unlinked binary and firing
# jobs for a package that is gone.
post-upgrade|service-restart|crond
pre-remove|service-stop|crond
pre-remove|service-disable|crond
